172
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:36,400
The first 16,000 vehicles rolled off the Ford and Willys Overland assembly lines in November 1941.

173
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:41,020
Manufacturers experimented with names for the vehicle,

174
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:44,120
like Blitz Buggy, Peep, and Midget.

175
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:50,320
But the Willys MB and Ford's GPW simply became known as the Jeep.

176
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:56,960
Based on the original Bantam design, the Jeep was an engineering wonder.

177
00:14:58,420 --> 00:15:03,080
What you're looking at now is a Willys MB Jeep.

178
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:06,780
One of the things the Army wanted were pioneer tools, an axe and a shovel.

179
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:10,040
Also down here, these are combat rims.

180
00:15:10,041 --> 00:15:14,840
If you had a flat tire, instead of using a tire machine, you would have to split these

